# Security response headers for the Cloudflare-served site (floodwarning.net).
# Cloudflare Workers static assets apply these to served files; the /api/* Worker
# routes set their own headers (see worker/index.js). GitHub Pages ignores this
# file, so the github.io copy is unaffected.
#
# Deliberately conservative: only headers that cannot change how the app loads
# its own resources. `frame-ancestors 'none'` blocks clickjacking without a
# resource-blocking CSP (a full script-src policy is a tested follow-up, since
# the app relies on inline handlers and several CDNs). See the security
# appraisal, finding M-3.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

# The Radio Path Maps tab shows these PDFs in an <iframe> on this same site,
# and the rule above (DENY / frame-ancestors 'none') stopped it: every map
# opened as "refused to connect". Framing by the site itself only — another
# site still cannot. A later rule's `!` detaches what /* attached, then the
# same-origin values are set (Cloudflare joins two values for one header with
# a comma otherwise).
/maps/*
  ! X-Frame-Options
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
